honeycomb-webrtc patch to webrtc-build m150.7871.04 (717ec1d), D82.

build/apple/xcframework.sh builds 11 slices (iOS, simulator x64, macOS, Catalyst, tvOS,
visionOS). This keeps the three the app ships and tests on, iOS arm64 device, iOS arm64
simulator and Mac Catalyst arm64 (the Mac app, honeycomb-ios Phase 5), with their dSYMs, and writes a normalised zip (fixed times, sorted entries, no extra
attributes) so two builds of the same input can be compared byte for byte, with the
xcframework's Info.plist listing its slices in a fixed order. GN arguments are
upstream's. The Catalyst slice links against the SDK of Xcode 26.0 (upstream's Xcode), given
by build.sh as CATALYST_DEVELOPER_DIR.

build.sh checks every file in UPSTREAM.sha256 before applying this with `patch -p1` in
the webrtc-build checkout. The other files listed there are used unpatched; they are checked so
a different upstream cannot slip in under the same pin. Re-derive on every webrtc-build upgrade.

